# PROVISIONAL Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TP1 profile, R adopted (2026-11-10; CUDA compat and engine 1a7ed13bb, 2026-11-11;
# engine 501674d7f, 2026-11-12; engine b62876185 with the inline mark and the quoted rule, 2026-11-13): the Phase 0
# proving model (plans/PLAN.md) on one Spark, with the architecture on. This
# is not a Qwen4 size and none of its numbers carry over to one. It is the control profile
# (qwen38-flash-next-tp1.env.example, the same prefill chunks) plus arm R of the lane-template rerun: tool-full, i.e.
# the compute lane with its server-side default, the in-model runner on the exact circuit and graph bank, and S3.
# Copy to profiles/provisional/qwen38-flash-next-tp1-tool-full.env (git-ignored) on the node and fill in the
# node-local values.
PROFILE=qwen38-flash-next-tp1-tool-full
RANKS=1
# The engine (since 2026-11-13, 20:00Z): upstream TensorFold aaac299d1 (vendor/TensorFold, unmodified) plus
# patches/series.tp1, every patch 0001-0083: the TP2 profile's set (0001-0080) plus three runner commits.
# (Earlier on 2026-11-13: f212eeabd plus 0001-0079, the measured tree; the README says what the base move
# changed.) scripts/build.sh tp1 applies
# them and builds this image. TP1 uses the upstream flashnext family (no
# TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE key), not Mia's engine. The three commits:
#   0081       after a digit stop fired in a reply, later reasoning digit runs stop at 64 digits
#              (TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_HOLD_MAX; this profile sets 0, off);
#   0082       no drawn word character glued to the ` @engine` inline mark (TF_RUNNER_MARK_STOP; this profile sets 0,
#              off);
#   0083       the quoted rule: an inline `<expr> =` or `A mod M =` inside an open quotation on its line is quoted
#              text, so the runner abstains there (reason `quoted`) and writes nothing (TF_RUNNER_INLINE_QUOTED,
#              default 1, on). The 4-bit model opens its reasoning by quoting the request; when the request held
#              `7^222 =`, the runner used to write the exact value into that quotation, the model read it as the
#              user's text, and the reply could run on into long invented digit runs.
# The digit stop and the 1,024-digit reasoning run cap (TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_STOP, TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_RUN_MAX) stay on at
# their defaults. The inline mark is on (TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=1): an engine-owned inline value ends in ` @engine`.
# The server runs with a default 8192-token thinking budget (SERVE_ARGS).
# Before 2026-11-13 the engine was qwen4/lane-template-toolcut at 501674d7f (qwen4/lane-template plus the cut
# tool-call fix), which the measurements further down name; it had both ChatML lane
# fixes, the reasoning-stuck fallback, the think-close turn (an answer left inside the think block a result turn
# reopened gets the template's next turn, thinking off, to answer in), the forced-rows fix (8522eb3a7: a forced
# result's rows all land before any stream hold), the runner in thinking chats only (1a7ed13bb, 2026-11-11: see
# TF_RUNNER_SPANS below) and the cut tool-call fix (501674d7f: a tool call cut by max_tokens inside a value ends at the
# bytes the value wrote; before, the cut streamed the closer's first bytes, "\n</"). Build its runner image (the
# native image plus the runner's frontend, calc.tfpc and the graph-v7-powmod bank, release runner-assets-20261107),
# then the CUDA forward-compatibility layer over it.
# CUDA driver (since 2026-11-11): the engine runs on the CUDA 13.3 user-mode driver (libcuda 610.43.02) over the
# Sparks' 580 kernel module, the layer ported for the TP2 candidate from Mia /
# MiaAI-Lab's NGC-based image. The image carries that driver's files from her image (cuda-13.3/compat/lib.real,
# libcuda.so.610.43.02 sha256 568153835562ea89c0c1669635e5631ada5f0862689025e3ed4a383086413e3a, the same 8 files as
# the TP2 image) in /opt/tensorfold/compat, and its entrypoint (tf-compat-entry, sha256
# 707096609e6ad7e112f081ade0f4014a2add7cb2607bbe9d32da98bac29c21d0) puts them first on the loader path only while the
# kernel module is older than 610 and cuInit succeeds through them; otherwise the host driver, as before. The boot
# logs which one it uses. TF_CUDA_COMPAT=0 forces the host driver. The engine binary is the same file either way.
ENGINE_REPO=https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold.git
ENGINE_REV=aaac299d1d90c2625e54cb50f3f0d1494c1c33ea
ENGINE_PATCHES=patches/series.tp1
# The patched tree is b62876185195's, the commit measured on 2026-11-13 (scripts/build.sh checks the tree sha that
# patches/series.tp1 pins), so every b62876185 measurement below applies to it unchanged. IMAGE is the tag
# scripts/build.sh tp1 gives the finished image.
IMAGE=qwen4-tensorfold:tp1
MODEL_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp1-tool-full-model-directory>"
# This checkpoint's own folders: never reuse another pack's prepared files, calibration or sessions.
PREPARED_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp1-tool-full-prepared-directory>"
STATE_DIR="<absolute-qwen38-flash-next-tp1-tool-full-state-directory>"
HOST=localhost
PORT=8000
CHECKPOINT=TensorFold/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MLX-4bit-MTP@2b170fa6309d5d1ee380b35636075fac7945f286
QUANT_FORMAT=mlx-q4g32
CONTEXT=65536
# The engine's serve flags, as measured: `serve <model> --host HOST --port PORT $SERVE_ARGS`.
SERVE_ARGS="--context 65536 --thinking-budget 8192"

# Prefill chunks (tokens), as in the control: 1536 while other requests decode, 4096 when a prompt runs alone.
TF_FLASHNEXT_CHUNK=1536
TF_FLASHNEXT_CHUNK_SOLO=4096

# Compute runs in the engine by default. With TF_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1 every thinking chat gets the built-in tool
# and the engine runs its calls itself, whatever tools the client sends: a harness cannot turn it off, and a client
# that declares no code_interpreter (opencode, for one) still gets it. The engine's own exceptions: thinking-off
# chats, tool_choice "required" or a named function, and max_tokens under 1024. Leave these lines as they are.
TF_COMPUTE_LANE=1
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT=1
# The in-model runner (the in-thinking path) on the exact circuit and graph bank, as the image ships them.
# TF_RUNNER_SPANS=reasoning (Flash-Next's default since 1a7ed13bb, stated here): the runner acts in thinking chats
# only, inside the think block. A thinking-off chat gets no runner session, so no cells and no engine-owned values;
# its reply is what the engine gives with the runner off. A thinking chat's answer after the think block is the model's.
TF_RUNNER=1
TF_RUNNER_SPANS=reasoning
TF_RUNNER_CIRCUIT=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/calc.tfpc
TF_RUNNER_FORMS=fence,repl,inline,trace
TF_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph
TF_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/graph-v7-powmod/bank/bank.json
TF_RUNNER_STATED=0
TF_RUNNER_INLINE_CHAIN=0
TF_RUNNER_INLINE_MARK=1
TF_RUNNER_SYNC_GRAPH=0
TF_RUNNER_COMPILE_STEPS=10522
TF_RUNNER_CELLS=1
TF_RUNNER_COMMIT=0
# The quoted rule (TF_RUNNER_INLINE_QUOTED) and the digit stop and run cap stay at their defaults (on). The mark stop
# and the digit hold are off: with the mark stop on, one lane-category item closed its reasoning at a mark and answered
# wrong; with both off the profile passed every check below.
TF_RUNNER_MARK_STOP=0
TF_RUNNER_DIGIT_HOLD_MAX=0
# S3: the lane's calls on the shared runner.
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER=1
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_CIRCUIT=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/calc.tfpc
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK=/opt/tensorfold/share/runner/graph-v7-powmod/bank/bank.json
TF_COMPUTE_LANE_RUNNER_SETTLE_US=3000

# Measured 2026-11-09 on one Spark, one boot per arm, the same pack and prompts. Arms: B = this file's chunks without
# the architecture (the control), L = B + the compute lane and its default, R = this profile. The P0 reference is the
# plain boot.
#   Check-suite categories the lane reaches (correct / items; tokens per item):
#                      P0 plain        B              L              R
#     arith  (40)      40 (566)        40 (566)       39 (803)       39 (894)
#     gsm8k  (80)      80 (428)        80 (428)       79 (362)       79 (362)
#     reason (40)      40 (1362)       40 (1362)      40 (784)       40 (744)
#     track  (20)      20 (3524)       20 (3524)      20 (1880)      20 (1832)
#   Thinking-off check set: 20/20 on every arm, no flips against P0.
#   Computation-heavy subset (12 tasks every arm started, 270 s each): correct B 4, L 8, R 9. B's other 8 ran out
#     of time thinking (about 4.4k tokens a task; L about 0.9k).
#   Arm proof (one modular exponentiation, greedy): L and R make 2 lane calls and give the exact answer, with drafts
#     on and with drafts off.
#   Decode tokens/s at 843 / 6k / 24k-token prompts: B 48.3 / 50.4 / 56.1, L 49.8 / 49.2 / 49.4, R 52.7 / 49.8 / 52.5.
#     4 streams at once: P0 83.2, B 89.7, L 86.5, R 90.8.
#   R's margin over L is within one boot's noise and its runner cells ran beside the lane's calls, so this does not
#   show what the in-model runner saves on its own.
# Receipts: the operator archive ltfix-rx-20261110 (per-arm smoke, arm proofs, speed, check-suite rows, compute rows,
# serve logs, the turn log and memory trace; ANALYSIS.md), kept with the private engine repo's run records.

# Adopted on the full validation, 2026-11-10, one Spark, R against B both on 37be6b28 (one boot per part, same pack):
#   Full check suite (797 items, thinking on): P0 plain 737, B 737, R 734 (R lost 5 items, won 2); no garbled replies,
#     no empty replies, no leaks; tokens per item P0 586, B 586, R 488 (17% fewer).
#   Computation-heavy subset (Study 1's 120 tasks, seed 101, frozen grader, 1200 s per request): R 92, B 50, both raw
#     (270 s) and at the raised deadline; B hit max_tokens on 70 tasks, R on none; tokens per task B 6605, R 908;
#     median wall B 234 s, R 20 s.
#   Thinking-off check set: 18/20 on both (P0 18), no flips. Smoke and the opencode replay pass on both.
#   Decode tokens/s at 846 / 6k / 24k-token prompts: R 50.2 / 49.0 / 53.5, B 49.8 / 47.4 / 49.5; 4 at once R 84.3,
#     B 87.6 (P0 83.2).
# Re-run on 751b92d4 (the reasoning-stuck fix), 2026-11-10: R's 5 check-suite losses, its 2 wins and 20 others, plus
#   20 compute tasks (R's 8 losses and 12 it got right). No item changed grade; nothing regressed. The 3 replies that
#   had ended stuck in reasoning (arith-40, track-31, dp-002) now return their text as content, with the right value,
#   but in thinking style: no "Answer:" label or bare JSON integer, so the frozen graders still mark them wrong. The
#   other 2 check-suite losses run out of tokens (8192); the 7 other compute losses give a wrong value.
#   Arm proof, smoke, opencode and the thinking-off set pass.
# Receipts: the operator archives ltval-rx-20261110 and ltre-rx-20261110 (ANALYSIS.md in each).
# Re-run on 969213b9 (the think-close turn), 2026-11-10, the same 47 items: arith-40, track-31 and dp-002 now score
#   correct ("Answer: 4253", "Answer: 20", "488"); no item went from right to wrong against R on 37be6b28 or 751b92d4.
#   Receipts: the operator archive ltre2-rx-20261110 (ANALYSIS.md).
# Full validation on c8e930375 (969213b9 plus the forced-rows fix 8522eb3a7), 2026-11-11, one Spark, one boot,
#   the same pack, against R and B on 37be6b28:
#   Full check suite (797 items, thinking on): 736 (R 734, B 737); won arith-40 and track-31 against R, lost none;
#     failure classes reasoning-only 5 (R 7), length 33 (R 33), nothing new; tokens per item 487 (R 488, B 586).
#   Computation-heavy subset (the same 120 tasks, frozen grader, 1200 s per request): 93, both raw (270 s) and at the
#     raised deadline (R 92, B 50); won dp-002 against R, lost none; no reply ended reasoning-only; tokens per task 908.
#   Thinking-off check set: 18/20 (P0 18), no flips. Smoke, the arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, ends on content) and
#     the opencode replay pass.
#   Decode tokens/s at 841 / 6k / 24k-token prompts: 48.8 / 47.8 / 53.8; 4 at once 85.1.
#   Engine gates: the full suite in 2 GiB + swap, 628/628 steps (9107/9382 tests, 275 skipped), test-golden 5/5.
# Receipts: the operator archive ltval2-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md).
# CUDA forward-compatibility driver, 2026-11-11, one Spark, one image (c8e930375 plus the layer), one boot per arm, the
#   same cells in the same order (Mia's decode protocol first on the fresh boot), cool-gated: R-host (TF_CUDA_COMPAT=0)
#   first, then R-compat (this profile).
#   Pre-registered speed score (geometric mean of 9 cells) +5.5%: Mia's protocol, median of 3 runs, aggregate decode
#     tokens/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 8 / 16 streams host 70.8 / 99.8 / 133.8 / 178.1 / 181.0, compat 70.7 / 102.3 / 137.0 /
#     182.4 / 183.2; decode at 847 / 6k / 24k-token prompts host 47.1 / 51.4 / 45.4, compat 53.6 / 49.5 / 55.3; 4 at
#     once host 83.9, compat 93.6. Single cells move several percent between boots on one driver.
#   The same requests gave the same tokens on both arms (the 72-item check-suite subset, greedy; 24 compute tasks;
#     the 20-item thinking-off set), so their wall times pair up: compat was faster on all 116, by 15% on the check
#     suite subset, 13% on the compute tasks and 12% on the thinking-off set. Against this morning's host-driver boot
#     (the full validation above) on the same items, the host arm was -1% to +9% and compat +11% to +25%, so the gain
#     is the driver, not the boot order.
#   Quality unchanged: identical replies on those 116 requests; check-suite subset 68/72 on both (68 on this morning's
#     boot), compute 20/24 on both, thinking-off 18/20 on both; smoke and the arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, ends on
#     content) pass on both. The opencode replay passed on compat; on host, turn 2 made a further valid tool call
#     instead of answering (a sampled choice; it passed on this morning's boot).
# Receipts: the operator archive ltcompat-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md, PAIRED.md).
# Runner in thinking chats only (1a7ed13bb: c8e930375, the packaging step, then this), 2026-11-11, one Spark, one boot,
#   the same pack, the compat image, against R-compat above (c8e930375):
#   Thinking-off check set: 0 runner cells and no runner block on any of the 20 replies (R-compat closed and owned one
#     value, in tc-comp-09); 18/20 on both, no flips; 19/20 replies identical, tc-comp-09 now computes the remainder
#     itself (still 4877, still correct).
#   Computation-heavy subset (the 120 tasks, frozen grader, thinking on, 270 s per request): 93/120, 120/120 replies
#     identical to the full validation's; 134 runner cells (140 there: answer-text cells never owned no longer close).
#   Check-suite subset (72 items, greedy): 68/72 on both, no flips, nothing new; 71/72 identical. arith-04 (thinking
#     on): R-compat owned two values in the visible answer ("+3125 = 3133... (4318 + 3125 = 7443)"); now the model's
#     own steps, the same answer.
#   Smoke, the arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, ends on content) and the opencode replay pass.
#   Engine gates: check-native-cuda-host, the host steps, fmt, lean and pr_check (0 new), gitleaks, the macOS compile
#     checks, the full suite in 2 GiB + swap (test and test-golden both pass). The new tests fail on
#     c8e930375's code (a thinking-off chat got a runner session; the answer triggered).
# Receipts: the operator archive ltspan-rx-20261111 (ANALYSIS.md).
# The cut tool-call fix (501674d7f: 1a7ed13bb plus 99518ecea, branch qwen4/lane-template-toolcut), 2026-11-12, one
#   Spark, one boot, the same pack, env and image recipe, against this profile on 1a7ed13bb (ltagent T, ltspan S):
#   Cut calls: 2 agent requests cut 7-10 tokens before their end, inside the last value, its framing newline or its
#     closer, streamed and whole: 12/12 end with finish length and arguments that are a prefix of the whole reply's
#     (no "\n</"). 1a7ed13bb has the TP2 engine's cut code: replaying TP2 agentshape2 mixed12k-s0-t1's cut, whose
#     bash command ended in "\n</", fails on it at runtime.
#   Agent cells (agent6k, agent12k, agent24k, 4x6k, 40 requests): 40/40 token-identical to T, replies byte-identical,
#     30/30 complete tool calls the same bytes. Speed: per request wall against T, median 0.999, summed 0.980 (the
#     4x6k first-token times move between its concurrent sessions on both engines; the walls do not).
#   Thinking-off check set: 20/20 replies identical, 18/20 on both, 0 runner cells. Check-suite subset (72 items):
#     68/72 on both, no flips, 72/72 identical. Smoke and the arm proof (2 lane calls, exact, ends on content) pass.
#     The computation-heavy subset did not fit the window (G down 20 of its 25 min) and was not run.
#   Engine gates: check-native-cuda-host, the new tool cut tests (they fail at runtime on 1a7ed13bb, 2 of 27), the
#     negative controls (both mutations caught), fmt, lean and pr_check (0 new), gitleaks, and the full suite in 2 GiB +
#     swap (633/633 steps, 1779/1851 tests, 72 skipped).
# Receipts: the operator archive ltcut-rx-20261112 (gates/, cut-C/, analyze.out).
# Release on b62876185 (the tree patches/series.tp1 makes), 2026-11-13, one Spark, one boot, the same pack, the
#   compat runner image, this file's env and SERVE_ARGS (window 10:25-11:16 UTC, no cuts):
#   Long-integer reasoning set (7^222; 3^300 and 2^500; 13^150; three seeds each): 9/9, 0 digit runaways, no reply at
#     max_tokens.
#   Computation-heavy subset (the 120 tasks, frozen grader, thinking on): 95/120 at 900 tokens a task.
#   Lane categories 179/180; check-suite subset 68/72.
#   Thinking-off check set: 18/20, all 20 replies identical to the earlier pin's (501674d7f).
#   Thinking-budget probe 12/12; tool_choice required, named and any pass; the opencode agent turns pass.
#   Not exercised in this window: no digit stop of any kind fired, so the stop after an owned value and the 1,024-digit
#   run cap were on but never triggered. One boot, one window: treat a one- or two-item difference as indicative.
